5. OPTIONAL MEMORY BEHAVIOR
==================================================

Memory integration must be configurable.

Default behavior must preserve current AG-001 behavior if memory is
disabled/unavailable.

Add validated configuration such as:

MEMORY_ORCHESTRATOR_INTEGRATION_ENABLED

and only other necessary settings.

Default:

false OR the safest existing architecture-compatible value.

Do not silently change existing production behavior.

Document the decision.

==================================================
6. FAIL-SAFE BEHAVIOR
==================================================

Memory retrieval failure must NOT automatically destroy an otherwise
valid orchestration request unless the architecture explicitly marks
memory as mandatory.

Define clear policies:

MEMORY_DISABLED
MEMORY_AVAILABLE
MEMORY_EMPTY
MEMORY_UNAVAILABLE
MEMORY_SECURITY_DENIED
MEMORY_TIMEOUT
MEMORY_INVALID_RESPONSE

For optional memory:

Memory failure
→ log safe failure
→ continue orchestration without memory

For mandatory memory, if introduced by policy:

Memory failure
→ fail closed
→ typed error

Do not invent mandatory behavior without justification.

==================================================
7. SECURITY BOUNDARY
==================================================

The integration must preserve AG-002 security guarantees.

Before memory enters AG-001 context:

- authorization already applied
- lifecycle filtering applied
- security-level filtering applied
- sensitive data sanitized
- snippets bounded
- metadata sanitized

AG-001 must never receive unauthorized memory.

Do NOT bypass AuthorizationService.

Do NOT directly read repositories from AG-001.

Do NOT expose secrets.

==================================================
8. ACTOR PROPAGATION
==================================================

Actor context must be preserved from AG-001 → AG-002.

Where available propagate:

- actorId
- actorType
- role
- organizationId
- workspaceId
- projectIds
- securityClearance

Do not fabricate missing actor attributes.

If required security context is missing:

fail closed for protected memory access.

