15. TIMEOUTS
==================================================

Memory operations must have bounded execution.

Do not allow memory retrieval to block the orchestrator indefinitely.

Reuse existing timeout abstractions if available.

Define:

- retrieval timeout
- context integration timeout

Do not create a competing global timeout architecture.

If AG-001 already owns the authoritative deadline, respect it.

Never extend the orchestrator deadline silently.

==================================================
16. CANCELLATION
==================================================

If the orchestration request is cancelled:

- memory operations should stop where possible
- no post-cancellation write-back
- no corrupted state
- no false success events

Use existing cancellation contracts.

Do not invent a second cancellation system.

==================================================
17. IDEMPOTENCY
==================================================

Repeated orchestration calls with the same request identity must not
cause uncontrolled duplicate memory writes.

If write-back is implemented:

- use requestId/correlationId where appropriate
- make operation behavior deterministic
- duplicate handling must be explicit

Read/retrieval operations should remain safe to repeat.

